---
/**
 * /live-web-photos/about. Live Web Photos, the fourth studio.
 *
 * Ported on 2026-11-16 from livewebphotos.com/about.html (five-studio
 * navigation, handoff section 5). The copy is carried over as written; Jon
 * edits it later. What changed is the frame around it: the studio strip, the
 * Live Web Photos nav, the ticker and the footer come from this site, asset
 * and link paths are relative to this address, and six class names that
 * collide with this site's own carry an lwp- prefix. Styles: src/styles/lwp.css.
 * Sliders, FAQ and scroll reveal: src/components/LwpScripts.astro.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Marquee from "../../components/Marquee.astro";
import LwpScripts from "../../components/LwpScripts.astro";
import "../../styles/lwp.css";
---

<Base
  title={"About Live Web Photos | AI Image Enhancement | North Jersey"}
  description={"Live Web Photos is a division of Live Web Studios — a North Jersey web design agency established in 2004. We bring 22 years of visual storytelling to AI-powered image enhancement."}
  canonical="https://livewebstudios.com/live-web-photos/about"
  ogImage="images/lwp/og-home.jpg"
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="theme-lwp">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">Our Story</span>
        <h1>22 Years of Visual Storytelling.<br>Now Powered by AI.</h1>
        <p>We didn't pivot to AI because it was trendy. We did it because the results are undeniable — and our clients were the first to prove it.</p>
      </div>
      <Marquee />
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:80px;align-items:start;">
          <div>
            <h2 style="margin-bottom:24px;">Where This Came From</h2>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">Live Web Photos is a division of <a href="../index.html">Live Web Studios</a> — a North Jersey web design and development agency I founded in 2004. For over two decades, we've built the digital presence of small and mid-size businesses across the region: plumbers, architects, law firms, logistics companies, contractors.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">The consistent thing across all of them? The clients who invested in their visuals outperformed the ones who didn't. Better photos meant more inquiries. Better product images meant higher conversion. A professional headshot meant more LinkedIn connections that turned into clients.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">The problem was always cost and access. Not every plumber can afford a $2,000 photography session. Not every realtor can wait three weeks for a photographer's editing queue. Not every e-commerce operator can justify $40 per product photo across a 500-item catalog.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;">When AI image generation reached a quality threshold where it was genuinely indistinguishable from professional photography — I stopped treating it as a curiosity and started building a service around it.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 style="margin-bottom:24px;">What We Actually Do</h2>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">We don't just run images through a filter and call it a day. Every project goes through a human-reviewed pipeline: the AI does the heavy lifting, and a real set of eyes approves every output before it ships to a client.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">We use a curated stack of AI tools — Higgsfield, Firefly, and others — chosen specifically for photorealism over everything else. If the output looks like it was generated by an app, it doesn't leave our pipeline.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">The standard we hold ourselves to: could this pass for a real photograph in a professional context? If the answer is anything less than yes — we redo it.</p>
            <div style="background:var(--color-bg-alt);border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:24px 28px;margin-top:32px;">
              <p style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-style:italic;color:var(--color-white);margin:0;">"The standard we hold ourselves to: could this pass for a real photograph in a professional context?"</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STATS -->
    <section class="section-alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px;">
          <div style="background:var(--color-bg-card);padding:48px 32px;border-radius:var(--radius-card);box-shadow:var(--shadow-glow);text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:3.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent);line-height:1;">22</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-mid);margin-top:8px;">Years in Business</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--color-bg-card);padding:48px 32px;border-radius:var(--radius-card);box-shadow:var(--shadow-glow);text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:3.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent);line-height:1;">48h</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-mid);margin-top:8px;">Standard Delivery</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--color-bg-card);padding:48px 32px;border-radius:var(--radius-card);box-shadow:var(--shadow-glow);text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:3.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent);line-height:1;">100%</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-mid);margin-top:8px;">Human-Reviewed Output</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--color-bg-card);padding:48px 32px;border-radius:var(--radius-card);box-shadow:var(--shadow-glow);text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:3.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent);line-height:1;">NJ</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-mid);margin-top:8px;">Based · National Service</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TECH STACK -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container" style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
        <span class="section-label">Our Tools</span>
        <h2 style="margin-bottom:24px;">The Technology Behind the Results</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">We're not a one-model shop. Different use cases require different tools — and the AI image space evolves fast enough that we're constantly evaluating and updating our stack.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:20px;">Currently we work primarily with Higgsfield AI for portrait and lifestyle generation, Adobe Firefly for product and composite work, and a proprietary review pipeline that ensures consistency across bulk orders.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--color-mid);line-height:1.9;">Every tool in our stack was chosen for one reason: photorealism. We're not interested in "AI-looking" images. We're interested in images that work.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section style="background:var(--color-accent-fill);padding:80px 0;text-align:center;">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:16px;">Send One Photo. See What Comes Back.</h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:480px;margin:0 auto 32px;">Send us one image. We'll enhance it free. No pitch, no pressure — just proof.</p>
        <a href="contact.html" class="lwp-btn lwp-btn--onfill">GET A FREE SAMPLE</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
  <LwpScripts />
</Base>
